# Decoding Video and Audio with Mediabunny

## Video Frame-by-Frame Decoding

To extract individual video frames as `VideoFrame` objects, use the **`VideoSampleSink`** class:

```typescript
import { VideoSampleSink } from 'mediabunny';

const videoTrack = await input.getPrimaryVideoTrack();
const sink = new VideoSampleSink(videoTrack);

for await (const sample of sink.samples()) {
	// sample is a VideoFrame object
	sample.draw(ctx, 0, 0);
}
```

You can also target specific timestamp ranges:

```typescript
// Loop between 300s and 305s
for await (const sample of sink.samples(300, 305)) {
	// Process frame
}

// Get single frame at specific time
const frame = await sink.getSample(42);
```

## Audio Decoding

For audio data, use the **`AudioBufferSink`** class to obtain Web Audio API `AudioBuffer` objects:

```typescript
import { AudioBufferSink } from 'mediabunny';

const audioTrack = await input.getPrimaryAudioTrack();
const sink = new AudioBufferSink(audioTrack);

for await (const { buffer, timestamp } of sink.buffers(5, 10)) {
	const node = audioContext.createBufferSource();
	node.buffer = buffer;
	node.connect(audioContext.destination);
	node.start(timestamp);
}
```

## Manual Decoding Control

For lower-level access, use **`EncodedPacketSink`** with the WebCodecs `VideoDecoder` API:

```typescript
const decoder = new VideoDecoder({
	output: (frame) => console.log(frame),
	error: console.error,
});
decoder.configure(await videoTrack.getDecoderConfig());

let packet = await sink.getKeyPacket(37);
while (packet && packet.timestamp < 50) {
	decoder.decode(packet.toEncodedVideoChunk());
	packet = await sink.getNextPacket(packet);
}
```

